  "chain": "PQI process bypassed [cause TBD, RC2] -> non-conforming resistor R2C installed -> resistor fails -> Analog Comparator 8 card malfunctions -> OPC circuit falsely actuates governor solenoids (20 1AG/2AG) -> turbine control & intercept valves close -> 100% load rejection -> reactor trip on OTDT / AFW-AMSAC actuation [mitigated by PORVs, AFW]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two root causes identified in parallel: RC1 (equipment failure of resistor R2C on Analog Comparator 8 card) and RC2 (personnel failure to implement PQI process allowing non-inventory material to be installed). Modeled fm_pqi_bypass as the origin failure mode leading into fm_resistor, since the PQI bypass allowed the non-conforming resistor to be installed, which then failed. Both RCs trace to the same official cause_code TBD/provisional category per form fields (cause code not assigned in FORM-366 FIELDS, hence provisional=true). AFW and RPS/AMSAC are systems the event INVOLVES (actuated), not backups in the BACKED_UP_BY sense — modeled as MITIGATED_BY since they responded to and mitigated the transient, not as pre-existing backups to an inoperable system. No previous similar LER found (explicitly stated), so no SIMILAR_TO edge/stub LER created."
}